# ==================================================================
# PRECEDENCE AND SCOPE
#
# Git applies the LAST matching line for each attribute, so the blocks below
# run general -> specific and the frozen-corpus block is last: nothing above it
# can reach app/, samples/ or diagrams/.
#
# There is deliberately NO blanket `* text=auto` rule. app/ is simultaneously
# the parity oracle, the field-contract source and the traceability anchor, so
# it must stay byte-for-byte identical. It is predominantly LF, but five members
# are CRLF-terminated - app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL, app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL,
# app/cbl/COACTUPC.cbl, app/cpy/COSTM01.CPY and app/jcl/CREASTMT.JCL - and
# samples/ holds six more. A blanket rule would renormalise all eleven on the
# next commit, corrupting the reference of record and producing exactly the
# sweeping diff CONTRIBUTING.md:33 asks contributors not to create. Every rule
# here is therefore bound to an explicit pattern.
#
# These attributes govern content conversion only. They do NOT set the
# executable bit: that is file mode, recorded on the files themselves (for
# example mvnw and localstack-init/init-aws.sh).
#
# VERIFYING A CHANGE TO THIS FILE
#   git check-attr text eol binary -- <path>   # what one path resolves to
#   git ls-files --eol                         # index vs worktree vs attribute
#   git diff -- app samples diagrams           # MUST stay empty
#
# FAILURE MODES TO AVOID
#   Never run `git add --renormalize`, and never add a blanket `* text=auto`:
#   either would rewrite the eleven CRLF members above and silently break the
#   fixed-width record offsets that the migration is validated against.
# ==================================================================

# ---- Java sources, build descriptors, resources and docs authored for the
# ---- migration: normalised to LF in the index and checked out as LF.
*.java          text eol=lf
*.xml           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.properties    text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf

# ---- Unix launchers and shell scripts: LF, or the shell cannot execute them.
# ---- mvnw is extensionless, so it needs a rule of its own.
*.sh            text eol=lf
mvnw            text eol=lf

# ---- Container and repository-hygiene files that carry no usable extension.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.editorconfig   text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# ---- Windows launchers keep CRLF, which cmd.exe requires for reliable
# ---- parsing. This covers mvnw.cmd; a second literal rule for it would be a
# ---- duplicate and could only drift out of step with this one.
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# ---- Binary assets: never EOL-converted and never diffed as text.
# ---- `binary` is Git's own built-in macro for `-text -diff`.
*.zip           binary
*.tar           binary
*.gz            binary
*.tgz           binary
*.7z            binary
*.jar           binary
*.war           binary
*.class         binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.eot           binary
*.PS            binary

# ==================================================================
# FROZEN LEGACY CORPUS - LAST BLOCK, SO IT OVERRIDES EVERY RULE ABOVE
#
# app/ holds the COBOL programs, copybooks, BMS mapsets, JCL members, PROC and
# CTL members, the CICS CSD, the VSAM catalogue listing and the data fixtures.
# samples/ holds the z/OS compile templates, the build procedures and two
# binary runtime archives. diagrams/ holds the legacy illustrations. All three
# are read-only reference material and must survive both checkout and commit
# byte-for-byte, so Git is told to perform no text detection, no EOL conversion
# and no diff-time transformation on them.
# ==================================================================
app/**          -text
samples/**      -text
diagrams/**     -text

# ---- The EBCDIC datasets are fixed-width records with NO line terminators at
# ---- all, so Git's NUL-byte heuristic would misclassify most of them as text.
# ---- They are marked binary explicitly and last, because the `*.PS` pattern
# ---- above does not match AWS.M2.CARDDEMO.DALYTRAN.PS.INIT.
app/data/EBCDIC/**  binary
